    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build succeeds and the full test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`). `AcceptanceBase` and `AuditLogCapture` are support classes; `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `bulkSignupWarning` on the create-owner flow, following the existing `namesakeCount` pattern (compute-and-stamp-on-entity, then map to the DTO so it also appears on subsequent GETs).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `bulkSignupWarning` boolean (readOnly) property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it by name automatically.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `bulk_signup_warning` column (`boolean bulkSignupWarning`, primitive so it's never null) with `isBulkSignupWarning()`/`setBulkSignupWarning(...)`.\n\n3. **Schema DDL** (hsqldb/h2/postgres/mysql) \u2014 added `bulk_signup_warning BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE NOT NULL`. Tests run on hsqldb; existing `data.sql` inserts use explicit column lists, so seeded rows default to `false`.\n\n4. **`CheckOwnerBulkSignup.java`** (new function) \u2014 mirrors `CheckOwnerDailyLimit`: counts pre-existing owners sharing the new owner's business-day-adjusted `registrationDate` (excluding itself) and stamps `bulkSignupWarning = count > 80`.\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new `checkBulkSignup` step into the pipeline (after `checkDailyLimit`, before `countNamesakes`), under the same `transaction` governance.\n\nFor a fresh single create the same-day count is 0, so the warning is `false` \u2014 matching `coreNoBulkWarningUnderThreshold`. The `>80` branch reuses the same daily-count accumulation path as the existing daily-limit rule; since the limit throws at \u2265100, the warning surfaces in the 81\u201399 band.",
